THIRD-PARTY DATA AND MODELS

This repository's own code is MIT.

* ProteinGym (Notin et al., 2023) - the DMS substitution tables used here.
  ProteinGym is released under the MIT License
  (https://github.com/OATML-Markslab/ProteinGym, and the dataset entry at
  https://registry.opendata.aws/proteingym/; both checked 2026-11-17). Each
  assay comes from its original publication, which should be cited with it.
  This repo does not vendor the raw tables: it commits per-assay summaries
  derived from them (results/*.csv, results/*.json); the per-pair tables are
  gitignored and rebuilt by scripts/build_pairs.py.
* ESM-2 (facebook/esm2_t33_650M_UR50D, Lin et al. 2023) - model weights under the
  Meta licence; used here read-only for a probe that failed to find signal.
* UniProt - queried live for sequence dates, not redistributed.
